;; M4T repeated occurrences: closure by self-join over the swept relation.
;; With the 3-cycle r0(1,2), r0(2,3), r0(3,1) the closure is all nine pairs.
;; Deleting r0(1,2) leaves only r(2,3), r(3,1), r(2,1): the sweep must
;; over-delete rec-founded survivors like r(2,1) (its foundation is zero and
;; it loses derivations through dying rows) and reseed them from surviving
;; recursive support, while the round-indexed partition keeps every lost
;; (r, r) instantiation decremented exactly once across rounds.

table (r0 int int)
table (r int int)

rule
(r0 X Y)
-->
(r X Y)

rule
(r X Y)
(r Y Z)
-->
(r X Z)
